# Jingle Bells, the chorus only (repertoire plan: jingle-bells). James Lord Pierpont's song of
# 1857, the chorus as it is commonly sung and printed, in G on strings 3 and 2 in first position.
# Notes: G = open string 3, A = string 3 fret 2 (finger 2), B = open string 2, C = string 2
# fret 1 (finger 1), D = string 2 fret 3 (finger 3). The teacher strums G, C, A7 and D7: G for
# bars 1-4, then C, G, A7, D7; G for bars 9-12, then C, G, D7, G.
title: Jingle Bells (chorus)
id: jingle-bells
composer: James Lord Pierpont
source: Song published in 1857 (first titled One Horse Open Sleigh); chorus arranged for Sixstring Academy
arranger: Sixstring Academy
licence: Public domain (Pierpont died in 1893); this arrangement is original to Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 2
tags: melody, lyrics, christmas, dotted rhythm
tempo: 100
time: 4/4
key: G

